    assert.equal(controls.textarea.disabled, Boolean(archived));
    assert.equal(controls.button.disabled, Boolean(archived));
    const before = writes.length;
    controls.textarea.value = 'Restored notes';
    await controls.form.fire('submit');
    assert.equal(writes.length, before + (archived ? 0 : 1));
  }
  assert.equal(savedTasks[0].notes, 'Restored notes');
});
EOF
cat >> README.md <<'EOF'

Each task row has a multiline Task notes textarea and Save notes button. Notes are plain text: saving preserves spaces, line breaks, Unicode and literal markup exactly; empty text clears them. Notes persist across reloads and restarts, travel with tasks on moves and returns, and leave all task fields, ordering, searches and filters unchanged. Searches still match only project names and task titles. Archived projects show saved notes with both controls disabled; restoration enables editing. Existing databases initialize notes as empty without changing existing data.

Notes checks cover schema migration, exact text and clearing, independent notes, archive restrictions, restoration, rename preservation, remembered move order, restart persistence, combined filters, search exclusion and failed-save recovery.
EOF
npm test"

